  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"0.196\"\n\npackage:\n  name: elfutils\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://fedorahosted.org/releases/e/l/elfutils/${{ version }}/elfutils-${{ version }}.tar.bz2\n  sha256: fd5cc6b77ad6773cac93cb3f415f9318ac3b3455eecf801f6b4a742c4f6c7209\n  patches:\n    - disable-werror.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip: not linux\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - pkg-config\n    - make\n    - gettext-tools\n    - libtool\n    - automake\n    # libcpu expands its instruction tables with m4 while building, so this is\n    # a build tool and must run on the build platform when cross-compiling.\n    - m4\n  host:\n    - bzip2\n    - libarchive\n    - liblzma-devel\n    - zlib\n    - zstd\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage('elfutils', upper_bound='x.x') }}\n\ntests:\n  - script: run_test.sh\n    files:\n      recipe:\n        - test_libdwarf.c\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n        - pkg-config\n\nabout:\n  license: LGPL-3.0-only\n  license_file: COPYING-LGPLV3\n  summary: a set of utilities and libraries for handling ELF (Executable and Linkable Format) files.\n  homepage: https://fedorahosted.org/elfutils/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - edisongustavo\n    - ehfd\n    - xhochy\n",
